# Scenario Analysis and Stress Testing

The platform should support controlled scenario experiments analogous to quantitative stress testing.

Possible scenarios include:

* Increased forcing intensity
* Reduced viscosity
* Reduced friction
* Longer forcing correlation
* Correlated forcing shocks
* Perturbed initial conditions
* Model-parameter combinations near unstable regimes
* Observation-system failure
* Missing sensors
* Increased measurement noise
* Reduced-order model mismatch

The system should calculate how these scenarios affect:

* Mean energy
* Mean enstrophy
* Dissipation distribution
* Extreme-event probability
* Forecast uncertainty
* Parameter-estimation accuracy
* Calibration stability

